# ArkUI Android

ArkUI-Project uses LineageOS 23.2 (Android 16) as its upstream. The manifest keeps upstream paths and revisions, with these development repositories hosted in ArkUI-Project:

| Repository | Source path |
| --- | --- |
| android | android |
| android_frameworks_base | frameworks/base (including SystemUI) |
| android_packages_apps_Settings | packages/apps/Settings |
| android_packages_apps_Launcher3 | packages/apps/Launcher3 |
| android_vendor_lineage | vendor/lineage |
| android_build | build/make |
| android_build_soong | build/soong |

Other projects use the remotes and revisions specified by LineageOS. Device adaptation starts by adding the selected device tree, kernel, and vendor dependencies to a local manifest.

## macOS source workspace

Clone this repository into `manifest/` inside a development workspace. Install `git`, `git-lfs`, and `repo` with Homebrew, then run:

```sh
./manifest/development/mount-source.sh
./manifest/development/sync.sh
```

The source tree lives in `source/`, mounted from `volumes/ArkUI-Source.sparsebundle`. Its APFS filesystem is case sensitive. The image grows as files are downloaded, up to 700 GiB. Run the mount script after a restart, before accessing the source tree.

Synchronization selects Linux host prebuilts, fetches selected revisions with Git LFS, and uses partial Git clones to download historical file contents on demand. The complete selected working tree is checked out. Run the sync script again to resume an interrupted download or fetch updates. Output is appended to `logs/sync.log`; successful synchronization writes `logs/source-lock.xml` with checked-out revisions.

To unmount after stopping processes that use the source tree:

```sh
hdiutil detach "$PWD/source"
```

## Linux build workstation

Use an x86_64 Linux host with a case-sensitive filesystem. Plan for at least 400 GB free disk space and 64 GB RAM, following the [official Android setup requirements](https://source.android.com/docs/setup/start/requirements).

On Ubuntu 24.04 LTS:

```sh
./manifest/development/bootstrap-linux.sh
mkdir -p source
cd source
repo init -u https://github.com/ArkUI-Project/android.git \
  -b lineage-23.2 --git-lfs --partial-clone --clone-filter=blob:none \
  --no-clone-bundle --platform=linux
repo sync -c -j4 --no-tags
```

Select a device and follow its [LineageOS build instructions](https://wiki.lineageos.org/devices/) before producing a flashable image. The source tree supplies the build toolchain, including Java. Initialize the build shell with:

```sh
source build/envsetup.sh
```

## Development and upstream updates

The sync script configures an `upstream` remote for each ArkUI fork and sends pushes to ArkUI-Project over SSH. Create a working branch for the project being changed:

```sh
cd source
repo start arkui-23.2 frameworks/base
cd frameworks/base
git fetch upstream lineage-23.2
git push arkui HEAD:refs/heads/arkui-23.2
```

Manifest development happens in `manifest/`, whose `origin` points to ArkUI-Project and `upstream` points to LineageOS. Review and integrate upstream changes before updating the manifest branch, then synchronize the workspace. Preserve upstream license notices in all source repositories.
